{
  "_comment_permissions": [
    "Permission patterns do NOT resolve most-specific-wins: a broad `ask` or `deny` entry",
    "shadows a narrower `allow`, and an `ask` in a non-interactive subagent resolves to a",
    "denial. So `Bash(rm *)` in either list silently revokes `Bash(rm agent_states/*)`, and",
    "the finalize monitor cannot honour its cleanup contract. Do NOT widen the rm rules to",
    "fix that \u2014 a glob permission is a string match on a command, satisfied by a `cd ..`",
    "first, a symlinked directory, or a shell-expanded variable. Allow the script instead:",
    "it resolves <git-root>/agent_states itself, refuses any other path, and takes no",
    "argument that can widen its scope. Keep the blanket rm deny.",
    "Both paths are allowed because a deployment may symlink the framework skills into",
    "~/.claude/skills rather than into the project. See .claude/skills/cycle/monitor.md.",
    "Both are also RELATIVE, and agents must call them that way. In fan-out 6 a monitor",
    "expanded the first into an absolute clone path, matched neither entry, fell through",
    "to the auto-mode classifier and was refused at Finalize."
  ],
  "permissions": {
    "allow": [
