  "_comment": "Sample hooks block \u2014 merge into your .claude/settings.json. Enables the per-agent event log at agent_states/events/<agent_id>.jsonl (consumed by run-report telemetry and stall salvage). gate-log.py on SubagentStop is what captures refused tool calls: PostToolUse never fires on a refusal, so a subagent denied a command leaves no trace anywhere else \u2014 fan-out 7 reported zero permission wait while three calls had been refused. Requires python3 on PATH.",
  "hooks": {
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "Bash|Edit|Write",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "python3 ${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/guard-framework.py"
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "python3 ${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/guard-secrets.py"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PostToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "*",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "python3 ${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/log-event.py"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "SubagentStop": [
      {
        "matcher": "*",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "python3 ${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/log-event.py"
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "python3 ${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.claude/hooks/gate-log.py"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "_comment_allow": "The allow list below is generated \u2014 regenerate with: deploy.sh grants. It covers framework scripts and the three artifact directories a cycle writes; add your project's own grants after it.",
  "_comment_file_rules": [
    "The artifact rules are spelled `Edit`, nested with `**`, and anchored with a single `/`.",
    "All three parts are load-bearing. Claude Code consults path rules for `Edit` and `Read`",
    "only: a `Write(...)`, `Glob(...)`, `NotebookEdit(...)` or `MultiEdit(...)` path rule is",
    "accepted, never matched, and warned about at startup. `*` does not cross `/`, so an",
    "`Edit(*)` covers the repo root and nothing below it \u2014 and every artifact a cycle writes is",
    "nested, which is a prompt per PRD, task file, state file and report. The single leading `/`",
    "anchors at the primary working directory, so one rule is correct in the main checkout and in",
    "every fan-out clone; a `//` prefix would mean the filesystem root instead.",
    "A docs vault needs more: its paths are outside the repo, so `deploy.sh grants <project>`",
    "emits `//`-anchored absolute rules for them plus a `permissions.additionalDirectories`",
    "entry. The allow rules alone do nothing \u2014 a path outside the working set is refused before",
    "any allow rule is consulted."
  ]
}
